# Private staging examples. Replace placeholders in an ignored local copy.
# Use the Vercel frontend origin so its existing /api/v1 rewrite preserves same-origin CSRF.
# Obtain each actor's session and CSRF value through normal verified sign-in + MFA.
# Never paste real cookies, signed links, bank details or evidence tokens into committed files.
@origin = https://staging.example.com
@base = {{origin}}/api/v1
@session = REPLACE_WITH_CURRENT_ACTOR_SESSION
@csrf = REPLACE_WITH_CURRENT_ACTOR_CSRF
@orderId = REPLACE_WITH_OWNED_ORDER_UUID
@bookingId = REPLACE_WITH_BOOKING_UUID
@refundId = REPLACE_WITH_APPROVED_REFUND_UUID
@aftercareId = REPLACE_WITH_REQUEST_UUID

### Public capabilities; draft/disabled states are server authority
GET {{base}}/public/capabilities

### Owned order: paymentDueAt/expiresAt and meta.serverTime drive countdown
GET {{base}}/customers/orders/{{orderId}}
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}

### Customer request: exceptional timing remains reviewable
POST {{base}}/customers/orders/{{orderId}}/returns
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason":"Please review this item and the documented condition issue."}

### Assigned/branch-authorized staff: approved capacity must already exist
# Set expectedVersion to the latest returned version; do not reuse this example's value blindly.
POST {{base}}/staff/bookings/{{bookingId}}/status
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"CONFIRMED","expectedVersion":1,"resourceReviewNote":"Recorded people and equipment availability for this appointment."}

### Staff receives goods; a separate INSPECTED request must precede return approval
POST {{base}}/staff/order-requests/{{aftercareId}}/review
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"stage":"RECEIVED","note":"Returned goods received and associated with this review request."}

### Refund approver: use a different capable account from the requester
POST {{base}}/staff/refunds/{{refundId}}/decision
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"decision":"APPROVED"}

### Refund transfer operator: request an evidence upload, upload the exact file, then record transfer
# Full upload and transfer schemas are in OpenAPI; use actual checksum/bytes and verified beneficiary.
# Only the original MANUAL payment accepts a bank transfer. Gateway refunds cannot use this path.
# POST /staff/refunds/{refundId}/evidence-upload
# POST /staff/refunds/{refundId}/transfer

### Independent checker: audited, short-lived evidence URL and decrypted beneficiary
POST {{base}}/staff/refunds/{{refundId}}/evidence-access
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Fourth distinct actor, REFUND_CHECK: only after actually checking evidence
POST {{base}}/staff/refunds/{{refundId}}/check
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accepted":true,"evidenceChecked":true,"note":"Independent bank evidence and beneficiary details have been checked."}

### Privacy intake does not perform deletion
POST {{base}}/customers/privacy-requests
Origin: {{origin}}
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind":"ANONYMIZATION","reason":"Please review anonymization of my account under the approved retention rules."}

### Administrator operational queues and expected worker heartbeats
GET {{base}}/admin/operations/status
Cookie: __Host-aat_session={{session}}

# Booking email URLs carry private, expiring purpose-bound tokens. GET renders a screen only.
# Its form POST uses application/x-www-form-urlencoded token + action=CONFIRM or CANCEL.
# Do not invent or hand-edit the signed token. OpenAPI documents both content types.
# Approved policy publication: POST /admin/policies (see exact discriminated schemas).
# Supply real signed evidence and calendars; this file intentionally invents no branch/zone values.
